-- title:
--   Speciality of the graded Cartier datum over W(k)/p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\iota \colon \mathbb{Z}_{p^2} = W(\mathbb{F}_{p^2}) \to W(k)$ be a ring homomorphism. Write $\bar\iota$ for the composite of $\iota$ with the quotient map onto $W(k)/pW(k)$, the quotient by the ideal generated by $p$. Let $\Phi$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $W(k)/pW(k)$, that is, a commutative two-dimensional formal group $F$ together with an action of $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ by endomorphisms of $F$ and an endomorphism $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi \circ \varpi = [p]$ and $\varpi \circ a = \sigma(a) \circ \varpi$ for the Frobenius $\sigma$ of $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$. Assume $\Phi$ is special for $\bar\iota$: its Lie pieces $\mathrm{Lie}_0$ and $\mathrm{Lie}_1$ are complementary and each invertible over $W(k)/pW(k)$. Assume further that the graded pieces of index $0$ and $1$ of the Cartier module $M$ of $F$ are complementary additive subgroups, the piece of index $n$ consisting of those $f$ with $a \cdot f = [\bar\iota(a)^{p^n}] f$ for every Teichmüller element $a$ coming from $\mathbb{F}_{p^2}$. Then the graded Cartier module datum attached to $\Phi$ and $\bar\iota$ — the Cartier module $M$ with its Frobenius, Verschiebung, the operator induced by $\varpi$ and the two graded submodules — is a special Cartier module: there is a family $\gamma \colon \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to M$ with $\gamma_i$ in the $i$-th piece such that every $x \in M$ is uniquely of the form $\sum_i [c_i]\gamma_i + Vy$ with $c_i \in W(k)/pW(k)$ and $y \in M$, and $M$ is $V$-adically complete in the sense that every sequence $(x_m)_{m \in \mathbb{N}}$ in $M$ admits a unique $s \in M$ such that for each $N$ one has $s = \sum_{m<N} V^m(x_m) + V^N t$ for some $t \in M$.
--
--   This is the base-point instance of the statement that the Cartier datum of a special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ is a special graded Cartier module, in the form needed when the base is presented as $W(k)/pW(k)$. It feeds the analysis of the graded piece of index $0$ and of the rigidification of the canonical $\eta$-map over $p$-nilpotent bases.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_isSpecialCartierModule_toGradedCartierModuleData_wittVector_quotient.lean

